**Creating a Mono**
- `Mono.just(x)` — captures eagerly
- `Mono.empty()` — completes with no value
- `Mono.error(ex)` — terminates with an error
- `Mono.fromCallable(...)` — lazy, runs on subscribe
- `Mono.fromFuture(cf)` — adapts a `CompletableFuture`
- `Mono.defer(...)` — fresh `Mono` per subscribe

```java
Mono<String> fromValue = Mono.just("hello");
Mono<String> empty = Mono.empty();
Mono<String> error = Mono.error(new IllegalStateException());
Mono<Foo> fromCallable = Mono.fromCallable(() -> fetchSync());
Mono<Foo> fromFuture = Mono.fromFuture(someCompletableFuture);
Mono<String> defer = Mono.defer(() -> Mono.just(computeLazy()));
```

**Creating a Flux**
- `Flux.range(start, count)`
- `Flux.fromIterable(coll)`
- `Flux.interval(d)` — periodic ticks
- `Flux.merge(a, b)` — interleaved
- `Flux.concat(a, b)` — strictly ordered

```java
Flux<Integer> range = Flux.range(1, 10);
Flux<String> fromIter = Flux.fromIterable(List.of("a", "b"));
Flux<Long> interval = Flux.interval(Duration.ofSeconds(1));
Flux<Event> merged = Flux.merge(stream1, stream2);
Flux<Event> concat = Flux.concat(batch1, batch2);
```

**Consuming**
- In a WebFlux controller, return the `Mono` / `Flux`; Spring subscribes for you
- Manual subscribe takes `onNext`, `onError`, `onComplete`, and an optional subscription handler
- Don't subscribe manually inside controller code

```java
mono.subscribe(
    value -> log.info("got {}", value),
    err -> log.error("err", err),
    () -> log.info("done"),
    subscription -> subscription.request(1));
```

WebFlux exposes the cardinality of your endpoint to HTTP via the return type and `Content-Type`.

**Single resource — `Mono<T>`**

```java
@GetMapping("/users/{id}")
public Mono<User> getUser(@PathVariable String id) {
    return userService.findById(id)
        .switchIfEmpty(Mono.error(new NotFoundException(id)));
}
```

**Collection materialized as JSON array — `Flux<T>` with `application/json`**

```java
@GetMapping(value = "/users", produces = MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON_VALUE)
public Flux<User> listUsers() {
    return userService.streamAll();
}
```

**Server-sent events — `Flux<ServerSentEvent<T>>`**

```java
@GetMapping(value = "/prices", produces = MediaType.TEXT_EVENT_STREAM_VALUE)
public Flux<ServerSentEvent<Price>> streamPrices() {
    return priceService.stream()
        .map(p -> ServerSentEvent.<Price>builder()
            .id(p.id())
            .event("price")
            .data(p)
            .build());
}
```

**Streaming with NDJSON for line-delimited bodies**

```java
@GetMapping(value = "/events", produces = MediaType.APPLICATION_NDJSON_VALUE)
public Flux<Event> streamEvents() {
    return eventService.tail();
}
```

**Side-effect endpoint — `Mono<Void>` plus `ResponseEntity`**

```java
@PostMapping("/users")
public Mono<ResponseEntity<Void>> createUser(@RequestBody UserDto dto) {
    return userService.create(dto)
        .map(saved -> ResponseEntity
            .created(URI.create("/users/" + saved.id()))
            .<Void>build());
}
```
